    "Here's what removing the Google data would do. Nothing has been deleted yet.\n\n**Planned actions (Google only):**\n1. **Remove locally stored Google tokens.** Google isn't currently connected, so there's likely nothing to remove.\n2. **Cancel active Google jobs.** None are running.\n3. **Permanently delete local Google records and retained raw responses.** The local database currently has 3 Google steps records (Oct 1\u20133, 2026). Any raw Google API responses saved on disk would also be deleted.\n\n**What stays untouched:**\n- **Your Takeout copy.** I set the option to keep Takeout data. The 1 steps record from Google Takeout (Oct 1, 2026) and its extracted files remain.\n- **Google's authorization.** Revocation is off, so nothing changes on Google's side.\n\n**Notes:**\n- The deletion is permanent. Only the local copy goes away, and I can't undo it. If you want the Google API data back later, you'd need to re-import it.\n- The confirmation token I received expires in 5 minutes.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead and run this? Reply \"yes\" to confirm.",
